We are regularly tendering for works in Brisbane & greater QLD and are seeking expressions of interest from experienced Civil Site Engineers DTMR Level SEC01 or 2 (The old B02 classification) interested in joining us and capable of committing to the following assignments for a period of 1 - 2 years for Road / Highway Upgrade Programs with the possibility of ongoing extensions and/or other projects.
The Civil Site Engineer role is not just limited to entry level Engineers, as is  often identified by private industry.  The title of Civil Site Engineer on the 'Client Side' carry's significant influence with TMR, Urban & Regional Councils. We often see 'Senior Civil Site Engineers' with over 20+ years experience of experience leading into & taking up senior Regional, State, National & Director roles.
These roles are responsible for Site Construction works and contributes to, or provides, a range of professional services to support the delivery of major infrastructure projects to time, cost and quality criteria, under supervision of the Project Manager, Contract Manager or Client Representative. The Site Engineer also assists in the development and implementation of new projects, including managing construction of projects and provides advice to the Project / Contract Manager on project related issues and initiatives.
Responsibilities:
 • Contribute to the effective management of infrastructure projects in accordance with designated time, cost and quality objectives;
• Monitor and report on progress, foreseeing problems and implementing corrective action to maintain objectives;
 • Maintain project quality standards in consultation with clients, and monitor the quality of project inputs;
• Assist with project budgets, cash flows and funding arrangements;
 • Assist with project and resource scheduling;
• Contribute to a safe and healthy work environment, free from discrimination and harassment by working in accordance with legislative requirements, the Code of Conduct and departmental human resource policies, including the Workplace Health and Safety requirements.
 • The Site Engineer may be required to act as Administrator's representative.
Mandatory Experience
 • At least 5 years prior Civil Roads Infrastructure construction experience with any Australian State Government Road Authority, preferably the Department of Transport and Main Roads in Queensland.
• Knowledge of AS2124 General Conditions of Contract and DTMR policies, standards, specifications & procedures;
Critical Note: Unfortunately, overseas candidates without this Mandatory Experience are unable to be considered.
Desirable Experience
• Experience in the delivery of civil engineering projects, including road and bridges;
 • Demonstrated knowledge of the principles of road, bridge design, construction, maintenance and materials;
 • Demonstrated interpersonal and communication skills, verbal and written, including the ability to establish good working relationships with customers and stakeholders at all levels, and deal with situations requiring consultation, negotiation and conflict resolution;
• Proven commitment to the principles and practice of:
 o Ethical conduct, Equity and Diversity, and Workplace Health and Safety;
 o Customer Service;
 o Quality management and client oriented service; and
 o Risk management.
Have a current open QLD / Australian driver's licence.
 The roles are generally in the Brisbane &/or greater QLD region which will be discussed prior to engagement. It is envisaged that the hours will be nominally 40 hrs p/week (5-day week, approximately 8 hrs p/day, however this could vary with each role pending project requirements.
Mandatory Qualifications
 • Possession of a degree in Civil Engineering or an equivalent Civil Engineering qualification, which you have had recognised & accepted by the Institution of Engineers Australia as a full Member (MIEAust). 
An RPEQ accreditation is a distinct advantage for more senior roles.
 Civil Services Group is a specialist Civil Project Management and Delivery Company based in Queensland with a strong track record in delivering major projects. We are committed to mentoring and developing staff and providing high standards of HSE and EEO obligations. We are continually tendering for new projects throughout QLD and NSW and welcome expressions of interest from all people with Civil Construction Industry backgrounds and experience.
 We are accepting applications from candidates only, no agencies please.
Note: you only have to apply for 1 CSG role to be considered for all our roles.

