Mandatory Criteria
Experience working on Civil Roads Infrastructure Construction Projects either directly or indirectly for or with the Queensland Department of Transport & Main Roads on DTMR Projects & be well versed and experienced with their policies, procedures & standards, Or; alternatively, any Australian Road Authority, directly or indirectly.
• Computer skills in Microsoft Windows operating system, MS Word, MS Excel, file management and email.
• Demonstrable Computer or tablet based diarising or reporting software skills.
Mandatory Qualifications
 • Possession of a degree in Civil Engineering or an equivalent Civil Engineering qualification, which is accepted by the Institution of Engineers Australia as a full Member (MIEAust).
The sites can be located anywhere between Gin Gin & Rockhampton.
The projects typically are 1 - 2 year duration's with the possibility of extensions or transition onto other TMR / Council projects.
The proposed hours are normally 40 per week & usually dayshift, but can sometimes involve night or weekend shifts to conduct the works, but these will be discussed & agreed prior to each assignment. (If shifts are required, they are usually cycled alternately to provide relief).
Must have a driver's licence and have access to own transport to/from home to site & mobile phone. Own laptop will be an advantage.
Preference will be given to someone already living in QLD &/or willing to relocate to a regional coastal town, however we will consider DIDO & FIFO.
Strictly current Australian Residents only due to the client Quality Standard requirements. Sadly, we don't make the rules.
